  {
   "id": 503402,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/af92b16ca02084f4.jpg\" alt=\"This figure shows a cross section of a leaf. Label 1 points to the thin, topmost layer of the leaf. Label 2 points to the solid, single row of brick-shaped cells directly under the topmost layer. Label 3 points to the next layer from the top, which is a set of loosely-packed, brick-shaped cells. Label 4 points to the third layer from the bottom of the leaf, which contains loosely-packed oval shaped cells. Label 5 points to the second layer from the bottom, which is a single row of brick-shaped cells. Label 6 points to an opening between the brick shaped cells that opens to the external environment. Label 7 points to the two cells that surround the opening.\"></p>\n\n<p>If the stomata were sealed, what would happen to oxygen <span data-math=\"(\\text{O}_2)\">(\\text{O}_2)</span> and carbon dioxide <span data-math=\"(\\text{CO}_2)\">(\\text{CO}_2)</span> levels in a photosynthesizing leaf?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 989591,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{O}_2\">\\text{O}_2</span> levels would increase and <span data-math=\"\\text{CO}_2\">\\text{CO}_2</span> levels would decrease."
    },
    {
     "id": 989592,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{CO}_2\">\\text{CO}_2</span> levels would increase and <span data-math=\"\\text{O}_2\">\\text{O}_2</span> levels would decrease."
    },
    {
     "id": 989593,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{O}_2\">\\text{O}_2</span> and <span data-math=\"\\text{CO}_2\">\\text{CO}_2</span> levels would both decrease."
    },
    {
     "id": 989594,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{O}_2\">\\text{O}_2</span> and <span data-math=\"\\text{CO}_2\">\\text{CO}_2</span> levels would both increase."
    }
   ],
